{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians","id":570512,"title":"low humanity vampires as intelligent villians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-27T13:23:33-07:00","id":570512,"title":"low humanity vampires as intelligent villians","content":"I was recently watching a show with a great vampire villain who's character was more a manipulative, sadistic genius than an animalistic predator. He was blatantly inhuman and I thought a similar character would make a good antagonist for a VtR chronicle. Unfortunately, B&amp;S makes it pretty clear that at 1 humanity a vampire becomes an animalistic and at 0 he becomes a draugr and only operates on instinct; i.e. they're more non-human than inhuman. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of replacing that dynamic of a slide into animalism with a slide into something more like anti-social personality disorder. A vampire would become less <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">empathetic </span></span></span>and more impulsive as his humanity decreases, but not less intelligent. Loss of empathy would mean the social penalties apply as normal, but a character could have a Feign Humanity merit which would nullify those penalties. Instead of going animalistic at 1 humanity a vampire would become impulsive by acquiring the Jaded condition permanently. This would make the vamp unlikely to resist frenzy at 1 humanity and unable to resist at 0, but they could still have some control by riding the wave.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Ideas on how much the Feign Humanity merit should cost? Should I allow players to use this scale, and possibly redeem their characters by purchasing humanity dots after they fall to 0, or just use it for some antagonists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T14:26:23-07:00","id":570584,"title":"","content":"There's always The Other, from the R1.0 Chronicler's Guide. It's basically a thinking Beast, without pride or anger. Instead of fight-or-flight responses, it heckles or bribes you to take the options it prefers. It cares only about self-preservation and sustenance, and will coldly, logically go about satisfying those imperatives to the best of its ability, short- and long-term.<br /> <br /> Trouble is, at Humanity 0, that basically means feeding deeply and efficiently, shoring up the Haven, watching for potential threats, and not much else. The Other doesn't like other vampires, and doesn't participate in the All Night Society. It only deals with them if it can do so cleanly, quietly, and briefly (not necessarily peaceably, mind), as more involvement means more chances for conflict, so such a character would have to be convinced that immersing themselves into that kind of Hannibal plotting would be somehow either preferable to isolation or completely unavoidable.<br /> <br /> They're also not much more popular in the long term than a Beastly Draugr, since eventually you'll have not just a Draugr, but a <i>thinking </i>Draugr, hunting other Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T14:38:10-07:00","id":570614,"title":"","content":"Considering the only mechanical penalty essentially amounts to having a difficulty relating to humans, I think you're actually covered. The text about being Humanity 1 really is an indicator of how close to Draugrdom a Humanity 1 vampire is.<br /> <br /> Have them be Humanity 4-3 and have Banes, and you've likely got a stable and very evil vampire. One with cool weaknesses players could exploit, too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T14:53:13-07:00","id":570621,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I thought about using the Other as inspiration, but vampires which fall to it are too robotic for what I'm looking for. I guess the problem is since the consequence of a vampire character hitting humanity 0 is for it to be taken out of the control of the player, vampire's in that state tend to lack, well, character. For an NPC though, I was going for the option of a vampire becoming a complete monster without it also becoming completely predictable. That's why I like the idea of an inhuman vampire which can function like an amiably evil, gleefully sadistic serial killer, mostly passing for normal because of it's ability to manipulate others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:36:38-07:00","id":570650,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a H1 vampire work in that regard? I think it isn't until 0 that vampires get <i>30 Days of Night</i>. As an NPC, they would just be lucky on breaking points until they are dealt with by players. If you really have trouble making it work with a vampire then why not use a Strix possessed? They pretty much start out where you want the character to be. They can work with vampires if it suits them too, so don't worry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T16:27:33-07:00","id":570676,"title":"","content":"One of the v1.0 books (<i>Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead</i>, I think it might have been) had a section on the Draugr, with some alternative rules for Humanity 0 Kindred.<br /> <br /> Instead of just being nothing but Draugr, there were two options: the Mindless Beast, basically a Draugr, with some minor notes; and the Careful Predator who acted in certain more cunning ways in accordance with Virtue/Vice; I suppose that could be extrapolated to the Mask/Dirge setup these days.<br /> <br /> The Careful Predator version was still able to act with a limited degree of intellect instead of just being a mindless feral vampire, so that might just be what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> (After all, it's your game, so there's no reason you can't take some of the rules you like and run with 'em!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T16:43:35-07:00","id":570695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=570650#post570650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a H1 vampire work in that regard? I think it isn't until 0 that vampires get <i>30 Days of Night</i>. As an NPC, they would just be lucky on breaking points until they are dealt with by players. If you really have trouble making it work with a vampire then why not use a Strix possessed? They pretty much start out where you want the character to be. They can work with vampires if it suits them too, so don't worry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I had forgotten about Strix possession, that's a good idea. Can a Strix possessed kindred still embrace? I started getting tripped up over the embrace issue, because I was trying to bring in an antagonist which could embrace a lot of people over the course of his terrorizing the city. Low humanity vampires couldn't embrace more than a few without turning into Draugr. That was why I got hooked on the idea of a sentient H0 vampire. Since, the embrace now causes humanity loss, an H0 vampire could embrace at will because it has nothing to lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T17:13:59-07:00","id":570726,"title":"","content":"Draugr can be just monstrous beasts but they can also be more careful predators. The book that expanded upon draugr compared the careful ones to serial killers, capable of working within vampire and human society, though at a disadvantage, but otherwise not really fitting in.<br /> <br /> They're taken from player control because their sole motivation is blood. They have no aspirations, no real wanting for anything beyond basic Beast things. So they're not going to play politics or befriend people who can't help them get blood. They can still be cunning and, above all, dangerous, but when you take a vampire and flense the humanity from it you're left with the Beast.<br /> <br /> For <i>low </i>humanity vampires you have a ton more options. Both the Circle of the Crone and Belial's Brood are entire covenants that revolve around the idea of keeping their humanity low. The Circle because the Beast is a gift, but one that can't be fully appreciated without some humanity. And the Brood because the slow sacrifice of Humanity to the Beast allows them to fully realize their full potential. Then there's just the average vampire that has, one way or another, lost their humanity. A vampire who has remained isolated from others of its kind for centuries and seen the civilizations it was once a living human being in die and be replaced, or who believes themselves to be some sort of blessed blood god, as well as the bold ones who just embraces being a vampire over remembering their humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-27-2015, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T18:01:45-07:00","id":570745,"title":"","content":"A normal strix possessed vampire can embrace creating revenants which should serve your purposes, I think. If a powerful strix uses synthesis on a vampire then it seems like they can embrace with the same results as a normal vampire with the possibility the child has some special quirk or power.<br /> <br /> I haven't seen any draugyr presented that does exactly what you want. You could fudge things enough, but a strix would be easier. They don't have humanity to deal with at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T20:05:44-07:00","id":570846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=570726#post570726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Draugr can be just monstrous beasts but they can also be more careful predators. The book that expanded upon draugr compared the careful ones to serial killers, capable of working within vampire and human society, though at a disadvantage, but otherwise not really fitting in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're covered in Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead. But the analogy only works with vampire society, not human. The examples of &quot;careful predators&quot; they provide are consistently savage and atavistic. I'm going for a Hannibal Lecter type, someone charismatic, smart, and capable of manipulating humans and vampires alike. I'm also fond of the affably evil types like Angelus from Buffy, or William Herrick from being human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:30:42-07:00","id":570893,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:43:55-07:00","id":570903,"title":"","content":"I had an NPC based on the tv show version of Hannibal in the last game I ran. She essentially commit diablerie on slashers using a coil that allowed for the devouring of human souls. She was a member of a home made faction of Belial's Brood descended from teachings of Semiramis.<br /> <br /> But yeah, in second edition the strix seem made to fulfill this thing, the manipulators and 'affably evil' types that aren't vampires are strix.<br /> <br /> Have you read the examples of strix in the book, Vyrkolash?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:50:03-07:00","id":571467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=570903#post570903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an NPC based on the tv show version of Hannibal in the last game I ran. She essentially commit diablerie on slashers</div> </div> </div> </div>...wait, slashers or Slashers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T10:24:28-07:00","id":571641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=571467#post571467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...wait, slashers or Slashers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Slashers. She would encourage burgeoning ones, as well. If they ended up balking at going the whole way she'd just let them go. It hearkens back to the Slashers book, where Nimrod was depicted as a Slasher, and a particularly prominent one. Semiramis was an interesting historical figure that seems to have a lot of legend about her but was tied to being Nimrod's wife and mother. So I figured the faction would develop that would see Slashers as the children of Nimrod, the Belial figure in their beliefs, and they draw out the dark parts of the Slashers soul into themselves to feed and replace their humanity with it.<br /> <br /> The faction is very against diablerie against other vampires. Not that they were against killing other vampires, they just believed committing diablerie on them was tantamount to defiling your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Checked some notes. 06-28-2015, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:20:59-07:00","id":571703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=570903#post570903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you read the examples of strix in the book, Vyrkolash?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but not lately. Somehow it had gotten stuck in my head that the Strix couldn't embrace; probably because the description of the issue is vague and doesn't include a mechanic:<br /> <br /> &quot;Strix embodied in a vampire can attempt to Embrace, but without humanity to spend, their Embraces nearly always result in revenants.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've been re-reading the Strix examples and I definitely think I can rework &quot;The Baron&quot; into what I want. I just need to homebrew a mechanic for my own sense of consistency. Something like &quot;When a Strix possessing a vampire attempts an Embrace roll it's shadow potency plus the host's blood potency. Unless the roll produces an exceptional success the Embrace produces a revenant.&quot; Then, I'd probably add a dread power which allows a Strix to Embrace reliably or make Strix who're capable of synthesis with their hosts able to fully Embrace a victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T14:05:07-07:00","id":571859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=571641#post571641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>S</b>lashers.</div> </div> </div> </div>-shudders-<br /> <br /> U<i>hu</i>huh<i>hgh</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T23:14:04-07:00","id":572322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=571703#post571703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but not lately. Somehow it had gotten stuck in my head that the Strix couldn't embrace; probably because the description of the issue is vague and doesn't include a mechanic:<br /> <br /> &quot;Strix embodied in a vampire can attempt to Embrace, but without humanity to spend, their Embraces nearly always result in revenants.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've been re-reading the Strix examples and I definitely think I can rework &quot;The Baron&quot; into what I want. I just need to homebrew a mechanic for my own sense of consistency. Something like &quot;When a Strix possessing a vampire attempts an Embrace roll it's shadow potency plus the host's blood potency. Unless the roll produces an exceptional success the Embrace produces a revenant.&quot; Then, I'd probably add a dread power which allows a Strix to Embrace reliably or make Strix who're capable of synthesis with their hosts able to fully Embrace a victim.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could just run it like the Baron: He's been in that body so long that he actually does Embrace real (if not weird) Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T10:34:46-07:00","id":572883,"title":"","content":"What about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> Success: Revenant.<br /> Exceptional Success: Kindred.<br /> Failure: Weird Zombie Thing.<br /> Dramatic Failure: AUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUUGH.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"