rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LoL, that would give me an excuse to bring back Larva from 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Failure or Dramatic Failure level? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T08:02:08-07:00","id":573967,"title":"","content":"Failure. Dramatic failure and you get hideous vampire-owl-monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T09:16:28-07:00","id":574022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=573967#post573967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Failure. Dramatic failure and you get hideous vampire-owl-monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> heh,<br /> <br /> &quot;How did you know Alder Klein was possessed by a Strix?&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;Well, when his latest childe showed up at elysium sporting a beak and screeching like a howler monkey... it was kind of a clue.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T01:27:14-07:00","id":578396,"title":"","content":"Strix can work, but I think a Hannibal Lecter type can easily be made just with the right Banes. You got 3 of them, choose them carefully and think what kind of &quot;sin&quot; you want your villain to commit on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> Lets say... Heinous, spree, or mass murder; Creating a revenant and Impassioned violence. It isn't out of reason to think that if he's able to mass murder without losing Humanity, he's able to do any kind of murder. Now you have a villain that can kill, maim, eat the entrails of his victims and let all the Revenants he creates loose in the world without risking Humanity AT ALL. You just have to choose carefully the Banes. Assuming that the character already spent some XP during his unlife to recover eventual lost Humanity, this char could easily be Humanity FIVE just by not embracing full vampires and going to a human church every other weekend. Keep him from feeding from children and from get into trouble with much frequency, and he can remain Humanity 6. In fact, depending on how you run this character, he could go as far as Humanity 8 and still be a disgusting monster.<br /> <br /> If you don't want so much Humanity, take Mass Murder and Embrace (it's a NPC, you can), and you will NEVER have to worry about this guy becoming Draugr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T05:40:38-07:00","id":578637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/570512-low-humanity-vampires-as-intelligent-villians?p=578396#post578396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't want so much Humanity, take Mass Murder and <b>Embrace</b> (it's a NPC, you can), and you will NEVER have to worry about this guy becoming Draugr.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt you could take a Bane to protect yourself from humanity loss from Embrace. Embrace is not a Breaking Point, the humanity dot is a cost you need to pay to create a full fledged Vampire instead of a Revenant, there's no detachment roll with it. Allowing it, even on an NPC it would kick the mood and the setting in very bad places very hard, if you can't find an IG justification once the question come's up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":". 07-04-2015, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:00:17-07:00","id":579155,"title":"","content":"I would stick to creating Revenants with such character, and I know very weel you're technicaly right.<br /> <br /> BUT.<br /> <br /> The entire point of Vrikolash was to have a villain that can do such things without becoming Draugr. IF he want to do full Embraces with this guy (and I'm not sure if he want), he could do that as the only and minor GM Fiat. He could even use two Banes for that and declare this as precisely one of the misteries about the NPC: how the fucking HELL he managed to avoid the Toll of Embrace.<br /> <br /> When the guy is a NPC, you don't have to think that he can't do certain things because whatever. You have to think if bending the rules for him will improve your game. And if the answer is yes, how you can turn the bending of the rules proper in yet ANOTHER interesting plot. It's a win-win situation if done with caution.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, there's no Detachment Roll to any Breaking Point against Humanity 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-04-2015, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:30:30-07:00","id":579190,"title":"","content":"Titto, <br /> Monte,<br /> <br /> I'm going to be using a Strix, but your conversation got me thinking. With The Vast Dynasty (fifth coil of the Mystery of the Voivode) Embrace becomes a breakpoint at humanity 3. A bane could be taken for it, so an Ordo Dragon character could become capable of Embracing at will. Alternatively a character with The Vast Dynasty, could focus his banes on breakpoints at humanity 2 and 1 (torture, premeditated killing, mass murder, etc.), and hang at humanity 2 while embracing at will and being extremely horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:56:01-07:00","id":579204,"title":"","content":"Quite right. The whole point is that Banes can do a marvelous job at letting your NPC being heinous without risking Humanity. On V:tM it was done with Paths of Enlightenment, but I think that Banes did a better job at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}